--TEST--
`Template::fill` throws when a flat key such as `'customer.name'` and a nested key give the same placeholder, naming both: rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-template-fill
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Novis\Spreadsheet\Template::fill
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Template;
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Workbook;

var $design = Workbook::createInMemory();
$design->sheet("Invoice")->add(["{{customer.name}}"]);
bytes $template = $design->finish()->bytes ?? Core\Bytes::fill(0, 0);

// Both keys give the placeholder `{{customer.name}}`, so `fill` throws an error.
try {
    Template::open($template)->fill(["customer.name" => "Shop", "customer" => ["name" => "Blog"]]);
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
The data has `['customer.name']` and `['customer']['name']`. Both fill the placeholder `{{customer.name}}`. Use only one of them.
